    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d116">

                <pb facs="0162" n="152" sameAs="frus:frus1943v01/pg152"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.48/1500: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-04-15T16:00:00+02:00">April 15, 1943—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 15—11:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2646. For Sayre<anchor n="21" xml:id="d116-f1"/> from Lehman. Jackson advised
                    Gore-Booth that proposed $2,500,000 fund was assumed by us to be used for the
                    movement of refugees from Spain to other countries. This proposal was originally
                    put forth by Long<anchor n="22" xml:id="d116-f2"/> and Gore-Booth was advised to
                    consult Brandt, since question of movement of refugees being handled by that
                    office instead of O.F.R.R.O.<anchor n="23" xml:id="d116-f3"/> We believe that
                    consideration of the establishment of any such fund should be discussed by
                    Bermuda Conference. [Lehman.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d116-f1" n="21" xml:id="d116-f1-content">
                <p>Francis B. Sayre, Deputy Director, Office of Foreign Relief and Rehabilitation
                    Operations.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d116-f2" n="22" xml:id="d116-f2-content">
                <p>Breckinridge Long, Assistant Secretary of State.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d116-f3" n="23" xml:id="d116-f3-content">
                <p>Office of Foreign Relief and Rehabilitation Operations.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
